From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:54:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,d2365-pmic-gpio: Allow D2089 GPIO
 lines

The D2089 of the A7 iPads has the D2207's GPIO block: iOS 12
AppleD2089PMU addresses the configuration byte of line n at 0x400 + n
for lines 0-16 and reads the input levels at 0x63 + n / 8, as on the
D2207. The A7 iPads have their Smart Cover hall sensors on two of these
lines (Apple's device tree, /buttons function-button_halleffect{,1}:
lines 12 and 10).

Let a D2089 node also be a GPIO controller, with reserved ranges for the
lines the PMIC keeps. Its node stays an event controller first: the
interrupt and interrupt-controller remain required, and since which event
a line raises is not established, apple,wake-events stays disallowed.
The D2355 remains event-only.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml  | 20 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
index b7b7b45..e94db0b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
@@ -36,9 +36,10 @@ description: |
 
   The Dialog D2089 PMIC used with the Apple A7 latches the same 112 events
   in the same block as the D2207, and the D2355 charger PMU used with the
-  Apple A10X latches 80. Only those event controllers are described: their
-  GPIO lines and the events they raise are not, so the node is no GPIO
-  controller.
+  Apple A10X latches 80. The D2355 is only an event controller: its GPIO
+  lines are not described, so its node is no GPIO controller. The D2089
+  has 17 GPIO lines configured as on the D2207 (lines 0-16); its node may
+  also be a GPIO controller, whose lines are not mapped to their events.
 
   Interrupt 112 (D2089, D2207) or 240 (D2365), one past the last event, is
   the event line itself. Its consumers run on every assertion of the line,
@@ -97,6 +98,7 @@ required:
   - compatible
 
 dependencies:
+  gpio-controller: ["#gpio-cells"]
   interrupt-controller: ["#interrupt-cells"]
   apple,wake-events: [interrupt-controller]
 
@@ -109,9 +111,6 @@ allOf:
             - apple,d2355-pmic-gpio
     then:
       properties:
-        gpio-controller: false
-        "#gpio-cells": false
-        gpio-reserved-ranges: false
         apple,wake-events: false
       required:
         - interrupt-controller
@@ -120,6 +119,15 @@ allOf:
       required:
         - gpio-controller
         - "#gpio-cells"
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: apple,d2355-pmic-gpio
+    then:
+      properties:
+        gpio-controller: false
+        "#gpio-cells": false
+        gpio-reserved-ranges: false
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
